  "courseSlug": "chatgpt-bard-bing-complete-guide-to-chatgpt-openai-apis",
  "courseTitle": "ChatGPT & Generative AI - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37780020",
      "title": "Using LangChain Agents For Automation",
      "sourceHash": "1f584b3488e626e5c62b3cb8091e9f4ab1bd0918da10f76bb24a94d3d79ffefe",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.01,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "So we had a first introduction to LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 7.08,
          "en": "Now, things can become more interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.08,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "as soon as you start using chains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.75,
          "en": "to combine multiple actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.75,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "and you can learn more about chains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 17.07,
          "en": "in the official documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.07,
          "end": 19.02,
          "en": "Now here, I'm not going to explore chains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.02,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "in great detail though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "but instead, another pretty nice concept offered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 28.01,
          "en": "by LangChain, and that would be the concept of agents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 32.853,
          "en": "And for that, I'll build a Wikipedia research tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.17,
          "end": 38.58,
          "en": "Now, for this tool, we again need to set up OpenAI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.58,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "So I'll copy that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 43.56,
          "en": "from the previous tool and paste it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.56,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "But now, instead of the prompt template, we will import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 51.77,
          "en": "from langchain.agents and we'll keep this OpenAI import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 56.493,
          "en": "But from this agent's sub package, we'll import load_tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.043,
          "end": 61.626,
          "en": "initialize_agent and AgentType.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 65.94,
          "en": "And you can think of agents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.94,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "as things in your code that leverage these GPT models",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 75.03,
          "en": "to decide which action they should take next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.03,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "a bit like you saw it with Auto-GPT, which also decided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "on its own with help of these GPT models under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "how to tackle a certain problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 88.08,
          "en": "and through which steps it should go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 90.99,
          "en": "Agents here in LangChain are a similar concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.99,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "Here you just have a bit more control over them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "And for that, you can create an agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "by calling initialize_agent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "and storing the result in a variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 103.95,
          "en": "Now, every agent needs a collection of tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.95,
          "end": 105.81,
          "en": "which it can use though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.81,
          "end": 108.21000000000001,
          "en": "And for that you can use the load_tools function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.21000000000001,
          "end": 109.86,
          "en": "offered by LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.86,
          "end": 113.05199999999999,
          "en": "load_tools then takes a list of tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.05199999999999,
          "end": 115.41,
          "en": "and you can find the available tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.41,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "in the official LangChain documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "Here under Agents, Tools, you can learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 124.56,
          "en": "about this feature and about the tools that are available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.56,
          "end": 125.393,
          "en": "Now, you might think",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.393,
          "end": 127.821,
          "en": "that you should simply give an agent all the tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.821,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "in the world, but instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "you should actually only give an agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 133.71,
          "en": "the tools it's likely to need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.71,
          "end": 137.4,
          "en": "because if an agent has too many tools, there is the danger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.4,
          "end": 140.73,
          "en": "of the agent choosing the wrong tool and ending up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.73,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "in a broken or infinite loop state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "So here for this basic demo, I know that the agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.22,
          "en": "should be able to search Wikipedia",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.22,
          "end": 151.17000000000002,
          "en": "and conveniently, LangChain comes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "with a built-in Wikipedia tool, which you can load like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 157.503,
          "en": "by adding it as a string to this list of tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.61,
          "end": 161.82,
          "en": "And in addition, my agent here also should be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.82,
          "end": 163.53,
          "en": "to perform some math,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "which can be unlocked with the llm-math tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 169.713,
          "en": "which is built into LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.24,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "The load_tools function then also needs a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 179.46,
          "en": "where you pass the large language model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.46,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "that can be used by those tools as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "for this llm parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "so that these tools under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 190.113,
          "en": "can use this large language model if they need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "So with that, we've got these tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "This agent now is equipped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 198.45,
          "en": "with these tools by passing these tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.45,
          "end": 202.65,
          "en": "this tools variable as a first argument to initialize_agent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.65,
          "end": 205.65,
          "en": "The second argument then should be the large language model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.65,
          "end": 209.04,
          "en": "which can be used by the agent to, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.04,
          "end": 212.73,
          "en": "ask these GPT models how to tackle a certain problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.73,
          "end": 214.44299999999998,
          "en": "and to come up with a plan.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.46,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "And last, but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 219.72,
          "en": "you have to define which kind of agent it should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.72,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "You do this with the agent parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 224.79,
          "en": "which should be set to AgentType dot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 224.79,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "And then you choose one of the predefined types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 230.1,
          "en": "You can learn more about them in the official docs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.1,
          "end": 231.54,
          "en": "It's in the end, depends on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 235.56,
          "en": "whether it should be an agent that should ask the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.56,
          "end": 237.39,
          "en": "for more input in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.39,
          "end": 238.223,
          "en": "In that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.223,
          "end": 240.81,
          "en": "you might want such a chat conversational agent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.81,
          "end": 244.68,
          "en": "Here I wanna use the ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION agent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.68,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "which basically goes ahead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 249.48,
          "en": "takes an input without any examples and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.48,
          "end": 251.793,
          "en": "and then tries to solve the problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "You can also set verbose equal to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 257.37,
          "en": "as a last argument here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.37,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "so that the agent logs all the steps it's going through",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 263.34,
          "en": "so that you basically have more insights",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.34,
          "end": 265.023,
          "en": "into what it's doing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.89,
          "end": 269.553,
          "en": "And then here, I'll just fetch some user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 275.07,
          "en": "the Wikipedia research task as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 275.07,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "so that the user should describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 280.71,
          "en": "what should be researched on Wikipedia.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.71,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "And we could build a prompt template here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 285.42,
          "en": "as we did it before with LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.42,
          "end": 288.51,
          "en": "But here I'm happy to let the user enter the full prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 288.51,
          "end": 291.57,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll just get that prompt like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 291.57,
          "end": 293.46,
          "en": "And then you can use this agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.46,
          "end": 297.42,
          "en": "and execute the run function to run this agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 297.42,
          "end": 300.153,
          "en": "with that given prompt as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.2,
          "end": 303.45,
          "en": "And that's how easy it is with a LangChain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 303.45,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "to create a basic agent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 309.12,
          "en": "that will be able to tackle a problem you give it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 309.12,
          "end": 311.04,
          "en": "on its own by finding out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 311.04,
          "end": 314.673,
          "en": "how to best tackle it with the tools it has.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 316.47,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "So hereafter, saving this file, I can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 324.05,
          "en": "execute this code by running python wikipedia_research.py.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.39,
          "end": 327.12,
          "en": "And the first time you do this, you will get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 327.12,
          "end": 329.97,
          "en": "basically telling you that the Wikipedia Python package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.97,
          "end": 331.95,
          "en": "is missing and that you need to install it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.95,
          "end": 333.39300000000003,
          "en": "by running this command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 334.65,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "So make sure you do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 341.49,
          "en": "You pip install Wikipedia, and once you did that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.49,
          "end": 344.31,
          "en": "you should be able to successfully run this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.31,
          "end": 346.95,
          "en": "this wikipedia_research.py file in my case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 346.95,
          "end": 350.43,
          "en": "And then here I can describe my research task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 350.43,
          "end": 354.73,
          "en": "And here I'll write what's the current age of Biden",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 355.95,
          "end": 360.15,
          "en": "and how old will he be in 2024 and 2028?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 364.527,
          "end": 366.3,
          "en": "And if I now send this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 366.3,
          "end": 368.64,
          "en": "if I confirm this by hitting Enter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 368.64,
          "end": 370.68,
          "en": "LangChain and this agent goes ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 370.68,
          "end": 372.06,
          "en": "and basically makes a plan",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 372.06,
          "end": 375.12,
          "en": "on how to find out what the response is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 375.12,
          "end": 376.473,
          "en": "And in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 377.52,
          "end": 380.58,
          "en": "it chooses the Wikipedia action to look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.58,
          "end": 383.25,
          "en": "for Joe Biden and find Joe Biden's article,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 383.25,
          "end": 386.34,
          "en": "which of course, also contains the birthdate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 386.34,
          "end": 390.87,
          "en": "And it then is able to give me the final answer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 390.87,
          "end": 392.67,
          "en": "that he's 78 years old",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 392.67,
          "end": 396.123,
          "en": "and that he'll be of this age in these years here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 399.93,
          "en": "And that's, of course, a very simple basic example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 399.93,
          "end": 402.36,
          "en": "with a very simple basic agent here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
